cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use opendrs in research, please cite it as below."
title: "opendrs: PR risk score and blast radius for pull requests"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "error-path"
repository-code: "https://github.com/error-path/opendrs"
url: "https://error-path.github.io/opendrs/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  opendrs gives each pull request a calibrated 0-1 risk score from git history, the import graph,
  size and tests, so low-risk pull requests can be approved without a person. It is an independent,
  open-source implementation of the approach behind Meta's Diff Risk Score, and runs as a CLI, a
  GitHub Action and an MCP server.
keywords:
  - pull request risk
  - blast radius
  - just-in-time defect prediction
  - diff risk score
  - code review
